<div>Dear Robert Samuel White:<br>
<br>
Thank you for your interest in public records of Lane County Sheriff's Offi=
ce. Your request has been received and is being processed in accordance wit=
h the Oregon Public Records Law. </div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>Your request was received in this office on <strong>9/9/2026</strong> =
and given the reference number <strong>P015875-090926</strong> for tracking=
 purposes.<br>
<br>
Your request will be forwarded to the relevant department(s) to locate the =
information you seek and to determine the volume and any costs associated w=
ith satisfying your request. You will be contacted about the availability a=
nd/or provided with copies of the records in question. PLEASE NOTE: The Ore=
gon Public Records Law does not require a governmental body to create new i=
nformation, to do legal research, or to answer questions.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div><strong>Records Requested:</strong> To the Records Officer, Lane Count=
y Sheriff's Office:<br><br>This is a request under the Oregon Public Record=
s Law.<br><br>I am Robert Samuel White, date of birth April 11, 1977. On Se=
ptember 3, 2026, Oregon State Police produced its file on me under public r=
ecords request PR27478. That production contains an email dated March 27, 2=
026, 11:04 AM, from U.S. Forest Service Special Agent Matthew Oliver to Dep=
uty Evan Meyers at evan.meyers@lanecountyor.gov, subject &quot;Siltcoos WC =
Volunteer,&quot; copied to two OSP detectives. It transmitted my name, my d=
ate of birth, my driver's license number, my residence, my work schedule, m=
y duties, my correspondence, and my text messages, and it closed with a com=
mitment to &quot;keep you up to date.&quot; I committed no crime; the OSP f=
ile itself concludes as much. This request concerns what your office receiv=
ed, what it created, and what it did with it.<br><br>Unless otherwise noted=
, the period requested is January 1, 2025 to the present.<br><br>I request =
the following.<br><br>The March 27, 2026 email described above, with all at=
tachments, as held by Lane County.<br><br>All communications between any La=
ne County Sheriff's Office employee and Special Agent Oliver or any other U=
.S. Forest Service employee concerning me, the Siltcoos Work Center, or the=
 archive at oprdvolunteerabuse.org, including every update received after M=
arch 27, 2026.<br><br>All communications between any Lane County Sheriff's =
Office employee and any employee of Oregon State Police, including Detectiv=
es Jake Hyde and Jerred Nelson, Sergeant Sean Henderson, and Lieutenant Hal=
ey McQuillan; the Oregon Parks and Recreation Department; the FBI or any ta=
sk force; or any other agency, concerning me.<br><br>Every record in county=
 systems indexed under Robert White, Robert Samuel White, Robert S. White, =
Sam White, my date of birth, my driver's license number, rsw@rswfire.com, o=
prdvolunteerabuse.org, or the Siltcoos Work Center as it relates to me: CAD=
 entries, records management system entries, incident or case records, flag=
s, alerts, advisories, bulletins, briefing notes, and officer notes.<br><br=
>Any record reflecting a patrol advisory, instruction, or direction concern=
ing me or concerning law enforcement response at the Siltcoos Work Center.<=
br>All records authored, received, or held by Deputy Evan Meyers concerning=
 me, in any medium, including notes and calendar entries.<br><br>Any record=
 reflecting dissemination of my information by Lane County to any person or=
 agency.<br><br>Records sufficient to identify Deputy Meyers's assignment a=
nd patrol area during March 2026.<br><br>Administration<br><br>Fee waiver. =
I request a waiver under ORS 192.324(5). Disclosure primarily benefits the =
general public: these records concern how a citizen's personal file, assemb=
led over speech the reviewing agencies concluded involved no crime, was cir=
culated to a fourth agency. I have no commercial purpose. All records produ=
ced will be published in full, at no charge, at oprdvolunteerabuse.org.<br>=
<br>Acknowledgment and timeline. ORS 192.324(2) requires acknowledgment or =
completion within five business days, and ORS 192.329(5) requires a reasona=
ble estimated completion date where a response cannot be completed within f=
ifteen business days. I request both in writing.<br><br>Fees. ORS 192.324(4=
) prohibits a fee exceeding $25 without prior written notice. If a fee is t=
o be charged, I request that notice with an itemized basis before any work =
is performed, and the opportunity to narrow the request rather than have it=
 held pending payment.<br><br>Format. Electronic delivery, native format, w=
ith headers, recipients, timestamps, metadata, and attachments preserved an=
d intact.<br><br>Preservation. Please treat all records responsive to this =
request as subject to litigation hold. I have served notice of tort claim o=
n the State of Oregon under ORS 30.275; the Department of Administrative Se=
rvices holds claims P195403 and P195427. On September 9, 2026, I asked Depu=
ty Meyers in writing to preserve his copy of the March 27 email, its attach=
ments, and my correction letter.<br><br>Disposition. For each numbered item=
, please state whether responsive records exist, produce them, or cite the =
specific exemption claimed for each record or portion withheld, as ORS 192.=
329(2) requires. If Lane County is not the custodian of a category, please =
identify the custodian rather than closing the request as to that category.=
 ORS 192.311(2)(b).<br><br>Robert Samuel White<br>P.O. Box 334, Reedsport, =
Oregon 97467<br>rsw@rswfire.com =E2=80=94 458-230-1869<br>
<br>
You can monitor the progress of your request at the link below and you'll r=
eceive an email when your request has been completed. Again, thank you for =
using the Public Records Center.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>Thank you,</div>
